IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-definitions-benchmarks`

-- Tests for sfa-definitions-benchmarks.
-- Expected values are written from the text of the Act (the quote lines in the module under test), never from its output.

-- administering a designated benchmark: limb the act is controlling the development of the definition of a designated benchmark for the purpose of determining a designated benchmark
#ASSERT (`s 2(1) "administering a designated benchmark" the act is administering a designated benchmark` WITH `the act is controlling the development of the definition of a designated benchmark for the purpose of determining a designated benchmark` IS TRUE, `the act is controlling the development of the methodology of determining a designated benchmark` IS FALSE, `the act is controlling the review of the definition of a designated benchmark for the purpose of determining a designated benchmark` IS FALSE, `the act is controlling the review of the methodology of determining a designated benchmark` IS FALSE, `the act is managing any arrangements, processes or mechanisms for the purpose of determining a designated benchmark` IS FALSE, `the act is collecting, analysing or processing any information or expression of opinion for the purpose of determining a designated benchmark` IS FALSE, `the act is applying a formula or other methods of calculation to information or expressions of opinion in order to determine a designated benchmark` IS FALSE, `the act is monitoring and conducting surveillance of any information or expressions of opinion provided for the purpose of determining a designated benchmark` IS FALSE, `the act is providing information in relation to a designated benchmark` IS FALSE, `the act is necessary or incidental to providing such information` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
